AMI Maintenance and Lifecycle Management

The overall lifecycle you want to establish is:

                  Current Golden AMI
                         │
                         ▼
                 Patch / Update
                         │
                         ▼
                 Build New Version
                         │
                         ▼
                    Test / QA
                         │
                ┌────────┴────────┐
                │                 │
              PASS              FAIL
                │                 │
                ▼                 ▼
            Approve          Fix / Rebuild
                │
                ▼
          Release New AMI
                │
                ▼
       Distribute to Regions
                │
                ▼
       Deprecate Previous AMI
                │
                ▼
       Retain for defined period
                │
                ▼
              Delete

AWS has specific capabilities that support much of this lifecycle: EC2 Image Builder, Systems Manager Patch Manager, EC2 AMI deprecation, and Image Builder lifecycle policies.

1. Recommended patching frequency

This question is asking:

How often should we create a new version of our Golden AMI?

This is not necessarily the same as asking:

"How often should production EC2 instances be patched?"

Those are two related but different processes.

Example

You could have:

Golden AMI
     │
     ├── August 2026
     │      └── v1.0.0
     │
     ├── September 2026
     │      └── v1.0.1
     │
     ├── October 2026
     │      └── v1.0.2
     │
     └── Critical CVE
            └── v1.0.3
What should you research?

You need to determine whether your organization wants:

Option A — Monthly

Every month
     ↓
Apply approved patches
     ↓
Build new Golden AMI
     ↓
Test
     ↓
Release

This is usually a sensible baseline for OS/security maintenance.

Option B — Event-driven

Build a new AMI whenever there is:

Critical CVE
Zero-day vulnerability
Critical OS patch
Important agent update
Major security configuration change

Option C — Monthly + emergency

This is the model I would investigate first:

Scheduled monthly Golden AMI release + expedited rebuild for critical security vulnerabilities.

Don't put this into the final company standard until you've confirmed your organization's patch policy.

AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager supports scheduled patching and specifically supports patch policies across accounts and Regions. AWS currently recommends Patch Manager policies through Quick Setup for configuring patching operations.

